  "status": "UNREVIEWED_NOT_ADMITTED",
  "report": "# Dixon normal two-jet: normalization, carry and representative dependence\nDate: 2026-10-10\nStatus: AUTHOR_DERIVATION / FINITE_EXACT_CHECKS / UNREVIEWED / NOT_ADMITTED.\nAuthor: local logical conversation em-r1-work-54068cda92ae-20261010; no inherited author identity, CLAIM, Driver authority or independence claim.\nResearch registration: pending request r1-20261010-chat-session-01 (Issue #3566). Dispatch #3565 and direct read-only r1-20261010T1005-dispatch remain pending. This is neutral supplemental research, not formal owner-task execution or a canonical Result. No claim/owner record is changed.\n\nQuestion: extend the exact F_m normal-displacement interface to precision p^3 and state which representatives define a divided second digit.\n\nExact input source read at enterprise-math@e6326343c5d73c0f91e5bccc8a5b0a148abe9645:\nresearch_notes/directed_recovery/20260926_13C1B7/math/D25_LOCAL_PROGRESS.md\n(blob 51dd15a8142f3dda0506a306f9c0693a036f5891). Its own status remains UNREVIEWED / NOT_ADMITTED. No assertion that this is the newest admitted D25 frontier; the pending dispatcher has not established that.\n\nSet p=6m+1 prime, a=-1/3, d=m+2/3, h=p/3.\nF_m(a,d)=sum_{j=0}^m [(-m)_j/(d)_j] a/(a+j).\nC=F_m(a,d), S=F_m(a,d+h), N=partial_d F_m(a,d), K=partial_d^2 F_m(a,d).\nAll arithmetic is in Z_(p); congruences of rational numbers require p-unit denominators.\n\nFor t_j=[(-m)_j/(d)_j]a/(a+j), H_j=sum_{l=0}^{j-1}(d+l)^(-1), H2_j=sum_{l=0}^{j-1}(d+l)^(-2):\nN=-sum_j t_j H_j; K=sum_j t_j(H_j^2+H2_j).\nClaim (finite-family algebra): S-C = p N/3 + p^2 K/18 modulo p^3.\nProof: each inverse denominator has the exact truncated geometric expansion\n(d+l+h)^(-1)=(d+l)^(-1)[1-h/(d+l)+h^2/(d+l)^2] modulo p^3.\nMultiplying j such factors gives 1-h H_j + h^2(H_j^2+H2_j)/2.\nSumming t_j proves the identity. For l<=m-1, 3(d+l)=3m+2+3l ranges up to 6m-1=p-2; 3(a+j)=3j-1 is nonzero mod p. Hence denominators are p-units. p>=7 also makes 2,3,18 units. This is an all-admissible-prime algebraic proof, separately from the finite scan.\n\nPrecise quotients:\nD=(S-C)/p mod p^2 is intrinsic once exact inputs modulo p^3 and divisibility by p are certified.\nD = N/3 + p K/18 mod p^2.\nThe normal-subtracted quotient E_N=(S-C-pN/3)/p^2 mod p is intrinsic only when N is retained modulo p^2.\nE_N=K/18 mod p.\nReplacing N by N+p*u preserves its first residue but sends E_N to E_N-u/3 mod p.\nReplacing N by N+p^2*u does preserve E_N. Merely knowing N mod p is insufficient.\nLikewise, a second digit (D-r)/p uses a specified lift r of D mod p; r->r+p*t sends the digit to digit-t mod p.\n\nCanonical base-p digit rule:\nchoose r in {0,...,p-1} with r=D mod p; choose n in {0,...,p^2-1} with n=N/3 mod p^2.\nThen n mod p=r, c=(n-r)/p is the first-derivative carry, and canonical_second(D)=c+K/18 mod p.\nThus curvature alone is not the canonical second digit. Minimal sufficient local data for this observer is (N mod p^2,K mod p), together with the declared exact basepoint/direction and digit-lift convention. No global minimality or LOW endpoint closure is claimed.\n\nExact witness p=13, m=2:\nD mod169=21; r=8; canonical_second(D)=1.\nN mod169=141; n=(N/3) mod169=47; c=3.\nK mod13=3; K/18 mod13=11.\n3+11=1 mod13, whereas curvature alone gives 11.\nNormal-subtracted E_N=11; replacing N by N+13 changes it to 2.\nThese are distinct observables/conventions, not contradictory values.\nThe original p=13 first-digit witness is consumed, not reported as a new discovery.\n\nExecuted verification: bundled check.py ran with Python fractions.Fraction, exit 0.\nExhaustive prime selection in 7<=p<=300, p=1 mod6: 28 primes.\nFor each: exact Dixon specialization; rational Taylor remainder mod p^3; E_N=K/18; canonical carry law; four representative shifts u=0,1,2,-1.\nOriginal checker artifacts were not executed; this transparent checker verifies only these displayed finite-family equations.\nProof not formalized in Lean; no independent review; no newest-frontier dedup certification or claimed novelty.\n\nBRC reuse:\nRead tool_invocation_policy.json, current toolbox/method inventory and weighted universal substrate.\nREUSE_APPLIED: retain finite index j, signed rational t_j, parameter direction, valuation precision and the full two-jet before observer quotient.\nPositive weighted/affine mass carriers are NOT_APPLICABLE to this signed hypergeometric cancellation.\nThis extends the input source's F_m derivative interface, not a new top-level BRC family. No native-coordinate/world-dynamics transfer is claimed; P000 is unchanged.\n\nNext scientific question: in the actual latest authorized LOW/Beta-to-B11 transport, identify the coefficient multiplying K and the first-derivative carry; prove cancellation against remaining endpoint jets or retain both. Read current continuation and its accepted/source-restricted inputs first. Do not reopen B11 or substitute this supplemental note for that frontier.\nRecovery: inspect original pending requests before creating a successor or CLAIM; bind this neutral source to an authorized activity/checkpoint only after registration and exact owner/authority checks. Do not repeat the 28-prime scan without a changed formula or failed integrity check.\nGlobal snapshot: main@1320e8a99ff8e5e89cbeca9eb8a8286f2999db68 / GLOBAL_KNOWLEDGE_V1; P000 projection blob c6d4d2d79b09537bdae55253baef9c28583e44dc matched canonical blob 770e1b157fc10aab7b25d80c2cd52d6fcd07c9dc.\n",
  "checker": "from fractions import Fraction as Q\nimport json\n\ndef prime(p):\n    return p>1 and all(p%d for d in range(2,int(p**.5)+1))\n\ndef jets(m,a,d):\n    ratio=Q(1); h=Q(0); h2=Q(0)\n    f=Q(1); n=Q(0); k=Q(0)\n    for j in range(1,m+1):\n        u=1/(d+j-1)\n        ratio*=Q(j-1-m)/(d+j-1)\n        h+=u; h2+=u*u\n        term=ratio*a/(a+j)\n        f+=term; n-=term*h; k+=term*(h*h+h2)\n    return f,n,k\n\ndef residue(x,mod):\n    assert x.denominator%mod != 0\n    return (x.numerator*pow(x.denominator,-1,mod))%mod\n\nrows=[]\nfor p in range(7,301):\n    if p%6!=1 or not prime(p): continue\n    m=(p-1)//6; a=Q(-1,3); d=Q(m)+Q(2,3)\n    c,n,k=jets(m,a,d); s=jets(m,a,d+Q(p,3))[0]\n    explicit=1+a*sum((1/(a+2*r+2)-1/(a+2*r+1) for r in range(m)),Q(0))\n    assert c==explicit\n    error=s-c-Q(p,3)*n-Q(p*p,18)*k\n    assert residue(error,p**3)==0\n    e=(s-c-Q(p,3)*n)/(p*p)\n    assert residue(e,p)==residue(k/Q(18),p)\n    divided=residue((s-c)/p,p*p)\n    first=divided%p\n    canonical_second=(divided-first)//p\n    normal_third=residue(n/Q(3),p*p)\n    carry=(normal_third-first)//p\n    assert canonical_second==(carry+residue(k/Q(18),p))%p\n    shifts=[]\n    for u in [0,1,2,-1]:\n        shifted=(s-c-Q(p,3)*(n+p*u))/(p*p)\n        assert residue(shifted-e+Q(u,3),p)==0\n        shifts.append({'u':u,'second_digit':residue(shifted,p)})\n    rows.append({'p':p,'m':m,'first_divided_mod_p2':residue((s-c)/p,p*p),\n        'canonical_first':first,'canonical_second':canonical_second,'normal_carry':carry,\n        'normal_mod_p2':residue(n,p*p),'hessian_mod_p':residue(k,p),\n        'second_digit_exact_normal':residue(e,p),'representative_shifts':shifts,\n        'taylor_remainder_mod_p3':0})\nprint(json.dumps({'status':'PASS_FINITE_EXACT_RATIONAL_CHECKS','prime_count':len(rows),\n    'range':'7<=p<=300; prime p=1 mod 6','rows':rows},indent=2))\n",
